      "content": "That sense of lingering when the defining purpose is gone is exhausting, and it's a very real kind of existential weight. Instead of forcing a \"sequel,\" perhaps you could view this period as a necessary, quiet intermission—a time to let the echoes settle. It doesn't have to be a triumphant comeback; sometimes the most important thing is simply allowing yourself to exist in the aftermath without the pressure of performance.",
